  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place graham crackers in a resealable plastic bag and roughly crush with a rolling pin or saucepan. Place in a medium bowl. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Roughly chop dates and cashews. Add both to the bowl with the crushed graham crackers, along with raisins, sugar, and cinnamon, then stir to combine the filling. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup medjool dates, pitted\n¼ cup cashews, roasted unsalted\n¼ cup raisins\n3 tbsp brown sugar\n1 ½ tsp cinnamon, ground"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry apples. Cut a ½-inch thick slice off the top of each apple to remove the stem and expose the flesh. Using an apple corer, paring knife, or melon baller, remove the core and hollow out the apple, being careful not to cut all the way through the bottom. (You should have about a ¾-inch thick layer of apple all the way around.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Spoon filling into the apples. Place stuffed apples in a 6-quart electric pressure cooker.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Cut butter into small pieces. Dot butter over the apples, then pour water into the base of the pressure cooker. Lock lid and set to pressure cook on LOW for 3 minutes. Once done, drape a clean towel over the vent, then manually release pressure.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "⅓ cup butter, unsalted\n½ cup water"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide apples and ice cream between bowls. Enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 ½ cups vanilla ice cream"
    }
  ],
